# network-lab/.env — read only by `docker compose` when run from this directory
# (docker compose does NOT read src/.env — that's a separate file for the Flask app).
#
# Copy this file to network-lab/.env and set the SAME value as CLI_PROXY_PASSWORD in
# src/.env. This password gates the HTTP CLI proxy (network-lab/cli_proxy.py, port 8080)
# that runs inside each of the 10 router containers — src/app.py (host side) uses the
# src/.env copy to authenticate TO the proxy; the routers need this copy to start the
# proxy in the first place. Without it, cli_proxy.py refuses to start (fail-closed) and
# the "CLI Transport" panel in the UI shows 0/10 devices for every request.

CLI_PROXY_PASSWORD=
